# =============================================================================
#  RetailPulse — .gitignore
#  Principle: commit everything needed to REPRODUCE the project; never commit
#  data we do not own, anything regenerable, or anything secret.
# =============================================================================

# --- Raw dataset: licensed (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), 120 MB, reproducible by download
#     Download instructions: documentation/dataset_setup.md
dataset/raw/*
!dataset/raw/.gitkeep
dataset/interim/*
!dataset/interim/.gitkeep

# --- Cleaned data: NOT committed -----------------------------------------
# Phase 3 output is ~90 MB across 9 CSVs. It is a DERIVED artifact: running
# notebooks/02_data_cleaning.ipynb regenerates it byte-for-byte from
# dataset/raw/ in about two minutes. Committing 90 MB of regenerable data on
# every rebuild would bloat the repository permanently for no benefit.
# Regeneration instructions: dataset/cleaned/README.md
dataset/cleaned/*.csv
!dataset/cleaned/README.md
!dataset/cleaned/.gitkeep

# --- Archives (the source zip, and anything re-downloadable) ---
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar

# --- Python ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.Python
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*/.ipynb_checkpoints/*

# --- Spreadsheet lock & temp files (Excel and LibreOffice both create these) ---
~$*
.~lock.*#
.~lock.*
*.xlk

# --- Tableau data: NOT committed -------------------------------------------
# ~70 MB of CSV derived from the MySQL views and sql/09_dashboard_sources.sql,
# regenerable with scripts/export_tableau_data.py and
# scripts/export_tableau_sources.py (byte-identical output, MD5 in the
# manifests). Same reasoning as dataset/cleaned/: derived, and the dataset's
# licence (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) is better served by the Kaggle original.
tableau/data/*.csv
tableau/data/analytical/*.csv
!tableau/data/.gitkeep
!tableau/data/analytical/.gitkeep
# The manifests ARE committed: file names, row/column counts and MD5 only (no
# data), so anyone can confirm a fresh export is byte-identical to the
# validated files.
!tableau/data/_manifest.csv
!tableau/data/analytical/_manifest.csv

# --- Tableau workbooks and extracts: they embed the data ---------------------
# The dashboard is published on Tableau Public; the repository keeps the
# documentation, the generated calculated-field list and the screenshots.
tableau/*.twbx
tableau/extracts/
# Generated by scripts/build_tableau_workbook.py: it stores this machine's
# absolute data folder, so it is rebuilt locally rather than committed.
tableau/*.twb
tableau/*.twb.backup
tableau/*.twbx.backup
*.hyper
*.tde
*.twb.bak
*.twbr

# --- Credentials: NEVER commit --------------------------------------------
# Narrow patterns only. A blanket *.cfg would silently exclude legitimate
# config files such as setup.cfg, which is worse than the risk it prevents.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
kaggle.json
credentials.json
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml
config/secrets*
*.pem
*.key
mysql.cnf
.my.cnf

# --- Logs & scratch output ---
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
scratch/
tmp/

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Windows (in case this repo is ever cloned there) ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace

# --- Claude Code local settings (machine-specific permissions) ---
.claude/settings.local.json
